# Valgrind leak suppressions for the memcheck job (ctest -T memcheck).
#
# The bats CLI test (jwt_cli) runs the shell and helper tools with
# --trace-children=yes, so valgrind also traces bash, mktemp, jq and friends.
# Those system binaries report definite leaks of their own, which would fail the
# test for reasons that have nothing to do with libjwt. Suppress definite leaks
# whose stack passes through a /usr/bin binary.
#
# This is deliberately scoped to obj:/usr/bin/* so it can ONLY match the system
# programs installed there. libjwt's library, tools and test binaries live in
# the build tree, never under /usr/bin, so a leak in libjwt's own code can never
# match this suppression and is still reported.

{
   leaks-in-system-binaries-run-by-bats
   Memcheck:Leak
   match-leak-kinds: definite
   ...
   obj:/usr/bin/*
}
